From e5ad0752461f3df489b21079f914205c7549594e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pocoteto <p@x>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 03:59:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/12] to-tickets: every ticket carries a Proof line naming
 the real surface and observable result

---
 skills/to-tickets/SKILL.md | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/skills/to-tickets/SKILL.md b/skills/to-tickets/SKILL.md
index 9b77a01..b87dd70 100644
--- a/skills/to-tickets/SKILL.md
+++ b/skills/to-tickets/SKILL.md
@@ -29,7 +29,7 @@ Break the work into **tracer bullet** tickets.
 <vertical-slice-rules>
 
 - Each slice cuts a narrow but COMPLETE path through every layer (schema, API, UI, tests): vertical, NOT a horizontal slice of one layer
-- A completed slice is demoable or verifiable on its own
+- A completed slice is demoable or verifiable on its own, and the ticket says how (its **Proof** line)
 - Each slice is sized to fit in a single fresh context window
 - Any prefactoring should be done first
 
@@ -46,11 +46,13 @@ Present the proposed breakdown as a numbered list. For each ticket, show:
 - **Title**: short descriptive name
 - **Blocked by**: which other tickets (if any) must complete first
 - **What it delivers**: the end-to-end behaviour this ticket makes work
+- **Proof**: how an agent shows it works on the real artifact, not a proxy. Name the surface (browser route, CLI command, API call, script) and the observable result (the value, screen, or output a person would check). Add the test seam when one is obvious. "Tests pass" or "it compiles" is not a Proof.
 
 Ask the user:
 
 - Does the granularity feel right? (too coarse / too fine)
 - Are the blocking edges correct: does each ticket only depend on tickets that genuinely gate it?
+- Is each Proof something you would accept as evidence the ticket is done?
 - Should any tickets be merged or split further?
 
 Iterate until the user approves the breakdown.
@@ -79,6 +81,8 @@ Do NOT close or modify any parent issue.
 - [ ] Acceptance criterion 1
 - [ ] Acceptance criterion 2
 
+**Proof:** the surface to drive and the observable result that shows it works (plus the test seam, if one is obvious).
+
 </local-ticket-template>
 
 <issue-template>
@@ -96,6 +100,10 @@ The end-to-end behaviour this ticket makes work, from the user's perspective, no
 - [ ] Criterion 1
 - [ ] Criterion 2
 
+## Proof
+
+The surface to drive and the observable result that shows it works on the real artifact (plus the test seam, if one is obvious). Implementers verify against this before calling the ticket done.
+
 ## Blocked by
 
 - A reference to each blocking ticket, or "None (can start immediately)". Omit this section when blockers were set as native edges.
-- 
